<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Blanche I of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1387">1387</a>–<a href="/years/1441">1441</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Blanche I (1387–1441) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1425 to 1441. A daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-navarre">Charles III the Noble</a>, she was first married to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-i-of-sicily">Martin I of Sicily</a> and then, in 1420, to John of Aragon, later John II. On her death her husband kept the crown instead of yielding it to their son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-prince-of-viana">Charles, Prince of Viana</a>, which led to the Navarrese civil war between the Agramontese and Beaumontese factions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/blanche-i-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Blanche I of Navarre" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zarateman · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olite_-_Iglesia_de_Santa_Mar%C3%ADa_la_Real,_atrio_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
